                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1aa865eb-22e3-3f14-9415-f0ff1d164c26",
                        "entry_id": "db8152f8-fa9f-39c3-b519-c3aa9650bb75",
                        "glosses": [
                            "религ. последователь или представитель религии, основанной на обожествлении, почитании Солнца; тот, кто поклоняется Солнцу как божеству"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fa1502f9-a293-4eaa-88c1-e37f98614975",
                                "sense_id": "1aa865eb-22e3-3f14-9415-f0ff1d164c26",
                                "text": "…сирийские Ваалы тоже были солнечными божествами, в силу чего тот из них, который при Аврелиане (середина III в. по Р. Х.) был приобщён к римскому пантеону, и получил там имя бога-Солнца. Итак, было ясно, бывшие подданные бывшего Великого царя были солнцепоклонниками."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f94e00a6-c235-3097-8e4d-013eceb913a4",
                        "entry_id": "db8152f8-fa9f-39c3-b519-c3aa9650bb75",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен., шутл. тот, кто любит солнечный свет, охотно загорает и т. п."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4718cac6-f09b-4317-afea-5a71e5925039",
                                "sense_id": "f94e00a6-c235-3097-8e4d-013eceb913a4",
                                "text": "Вася, настоящий солнцепоклонник, блаженно прикрыл глаза ладонью, затем осторожно глянул вниз, на море."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0860a76f-5d55-4d77-8234-d96222ded8c9",
                        "source_entry_id": "db8152f8-fa9f-39c3-b519-c3aa9650bb75",
                        "target_lang_word": "sun worshipper",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sun worshipper",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "89e0aba7-303d-3cbd-9e9a-319b260d6e71",
                                        "entry_id": "f1b82198-9860-358a-9ebc-c53ba9377bcd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who reveres the Sun as a deity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff344ea7-3ff7-4e0c-89c3-2c6ebdb27fbe",
                                                "sense_id": "89e0aba7-303d-3cbd-9e9a-319b260d6e71",
                                                "text": "Here Christian, or Jew, Sun-worshipper or Pagan implore their several gods unmolested."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b49b34ff-d4ee-429b-90e4-a7f34e397f11",
                                                "sense_id": "89e0aba7-303d-3cbd-9e9a-319b260d6e71",
                                                "text": "He had fallen into the hands of descendants of the ancient sun worshippers. His seeming rescue by a votaress of the high priestess of the sun had been but a part of the mimicry of their heathen ceremony—the sun looking down upon him through the opening at the top of the court had claimed him as his own, and the priestess had come from the inner temple to save him from the polluting hands of worldlings—to save him as a human offering to their flaming deity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38802edd-7b7f-498b-8950-cf38e5b6c1d9",
                                                "sense_id": "89e0aba7-303d-3cbd-9e9a-319b260d6e71",
                                                "text": "Moses warns his followers against the allure of sun- and star-worship; and Ezekiel mentions seeing, in a vision, twenty-five men of Judah worshipping the sun. Indeed, so powerful was the incentive to worship the sun, and so great was its rivalry to the worship of Jehovah, that it was found necessary to take the most drastic measures towards its suppression. Sun-worshippers were threatened with death by stoning."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "07beb25c-89b7-3e4f-8202-26e9917315a3",
                                        "entry_id": "f1b82198-9860-358a-9ebc-c53ba9377bcd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who enjoys exposure to sunlight; an avid sunbather."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9be93a69-412e-4b99-a2dd-ed7592d2a656",
                                                "sense_id": "07beb25c-89b7-3e4f-8202-26e9917315a3",
                                                "text": "\"The light hurts you?\" she said, for the sun was coming into the room. \"Change places with me, I am a sun worshipper.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d0958b6-5b8d-4725-9337-0da465c361fd",
                                                "sense_id": "07beb25c-89b7-3e4f-8202-26e9917315a3",
                                                "text": "A bikini . . . tends to slip and slide a bit in the surf. But for a die-hard sun worshipper, a two-piece suit is the next best thing to nothing at all."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d70f381-c46f-42ee-97b1-68eecee6b750",
                                                "sense_id": "07beb25c-89b7-3e4f-8202-26e9917315a3",
                                                "text": "Previous research by Rees has confirmed what sun worshippers already knew: that the upper back is much more likely to tan than the legs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c2aad172-5181-4f00-8996-331b49130656",
